# Roadmap and decision gates

## Now: v0.1 research prototype

- [x] Define a narrow project and explicit non-goals.
- [x] Draft schema, validator, synthetic examples, tests, and research protocol.
- [x] Keep real evidence and real incident reports out of the repository.
- [x] Prepare a private consultation issue memo and a grant draft.
- [ ] Execute and independently reproduce the full test suite.
- [ ] Review the complete FMIR proposal before any public comment.
- [ ] Obtain technical and governance critique.

## Gate 1: reproducible artifact

Advance only when a clean-environment run is recorded, independent schema validation agrees on the fixtures, and serious correctness defects are resolved. Failure leads to repair or abandonment, not a stronger public claim.

## Gate 2: useful to intended users

Conduct Stage 1 interviews and revise the fields. If users consistently find that the structure obscures uncertainty or adds unjustified burden, simplify or stop. Do not solicit real confidential incidents.

## Gate 3: comparative evidence

Run the small counterbalanced synthetic study only after ethics, privacy, and reproducibility checks. Publish protocol deviations and negative results. The sample can guide redesign, not prove regulatory or safety benefit.

## Later possibilities, not commitments

- adapters to existing reporting formats after a documented mapping review;
- secure evidence-reference verification after a separate security design;
- multilingual and accessibility review;
- larger independent replication;
- work on evaluation reproducibility or autonomous-agent evaluations if evidence and collaborators suggest a better marginal contribution.

## Explicitly out of scope for this phase

- a general newsletter or undifferentiated public-awareness campaign;
- public signing, press quotes, or named advocacy before Morgan's employment review;
- hosting real incident submissions or sensitive evidence;
- claiming compliance, safety certification, or regulatory endorsement;
- spending money or submitting financial commitments without Morgan's approval;
- expanding into an umbrella organization before the first artifact is reproduced and criticized.

# Contributing

IEK is currently an unaudited research prototype. The most valuable early contribution is criticism that can be checked, not endorsement.

## Useful contributions

- execute the documented tests and report exact environment and output;
- find false validation results or cases where warnings obscure a real ambiguity;
- compare the schema with a primary-source reporting format;
- critique field definitions from technical, governance, security, accessibility, or affected-party perspectives;
- contribute synthetic edge cases with no real provider, person, vulnerability, or confidential detail.

## Do not submit

- real incident reports, logs, prompts, credentials, personal data, or evidence bundles;
- operational instructions for harmful behavior;
- claims that validation proves compliance, truth, or safety;
- fabricated reviewer feedback, study participants, results, citations, or incident records.

## Changes

Update the schema version, examples, tests, design notes, and verification log together when changing semantics. Preserve historical interpretations in a changelog. Record disagreements and negative results rather than resolving them silently.

AI assistance must be disclosed in research outputs. A human accountable for the work must review any external submission, data analysis, or safety-relevant claim.

:root {
  color-scheme: light;
  --ink: #142b2a;
  --muted: #526664;
  --paper: #f7f5ee;
  --tint: #e9efe9;
  --line: #c8d3ca;
  --accent: #b44a32;
  --accent-dark: #863421;
  --focus: #155eef;
  --max: 1120px;
  font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  font-synthesis: none;
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.65; }
a { color: var(--accent-dark); text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
a:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 4px; }
.skip-link { position: absolute; left: 1rem; top: -5rem; background: var(--ink); color: white; padding: 0.7rem 1rem; z-index: 10; }
.skip-link:focus { top: 1rem; }

.site-header, main, footer { width: min(var(--max), calc(100% - 3rem)); margin-inline: auto; }
.site-header { min-height: 6rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
.wordmark { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 760; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
.status { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.82rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
.status a { color: var(--muted); }

.hero { padding: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 8rem) 0 clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem); max-width: 940px; }
.eyebrow, .section-number { color: var(--accent-dark); font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 760; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
h1, h2, h3 { line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.035em; }
h1 { max-width: 920px; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7.2vw, 5.9rem); font-weight: 650; }
h1 em { font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; font-weight: 400; color: var(--accent-dark); }
h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 600; }
h3 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 0.7rem 0; }
.lede { max-width: 760px; color: var(--muted); font-size: clamp(1.12rem, 2vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.6; }
.actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
.button { display: inline-block; background: var(--ink); color: white; padding: 0.85rem 1.2rem; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 3px; font-weight: 650; }
.button:hover { background: #244743; }
.text-link { font-weight: 650; }

.notice { border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); background: #f1e9df; padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
.notice p { margin: 0.4rem 0 0; max-width: 900px; }
.section { padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
.section-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(240px, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem); align-items: start; }
.section-number { margin: 0 0 2rem; }
.tinted { position: relative; }
.tinted::before { content: ""; position: absolute; z-index: -1; inset: 0 calc((100vw - min(var(--max), calc(100vw - 3rem))) / -2); background: var(--tint); }
.prose { max-width: 680px; }
.prose > p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
.prose p { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
.fine-print { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }

.cards { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
.card { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.55); border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem; }
.card p { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--muted); }
.card-index { color: var(--accent-dark); font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.2rem; }
pre { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; padding: 1.2rem; background: var(--ink); color: #f1f4eb; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; }
code { font-family: "SFMono-Regular", Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace; }
.feature-list { padding-left: 1.3rem; }
.feature-list li { margin: 0.45rem 0; }
details { margin-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 1rem; }
summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700; }
.contribute { padding-bottom: 7rem; }

footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 2rem 0 3rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; }
footer p { margin: 0.35rem 0; }

.document { max-width: 820px; }
.document > h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); margin-top: 1rem; }
.document > .eyebrow { margin-top: 5rem; }
.document section { padding: 2.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
.document h2 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.5vw, 2.4rem); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
.document li { margin: 0.65rem 0; }
.contents { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; margin: 2.5rem 0; padding: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
.contents strong { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
.definitions { margin: 0; }
.definitions div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr); gap: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1rem 0; }
.definitions dt { font-weight: 700; }
.definitions dd { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }

@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .site-header, main, footer { width: min(100% - 2rem, var(--max)); }
  .site-header { min-height: 5rem; align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 0.2rem; padding: 0.8rem 0; }
  .section-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .section-number { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .definitions div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.3rem; }
  .hero { padding-top: 4rem; }
  .tinted::before { inset-inline: -1rem; }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
}

@media print {
  body { background: white; color: black; font-size: 11pt; }
  .site-header, .skip-link, .actions, footer { display: none; }
  main { width: 100%; }
  .hero, .document > .eyebrow { padding-top: 0; margin-top: 0; }
  .section, .document section { break-inside: avoid; }
  a { color: black; }
}
